# CODEOWNERS — the owner-gated surfaces (PRD 7.5, rule R-H).
#
# Agents merge their own work when CI is green EXCEPT on these paths, where a
# mistake is expensive or irreversible: settled architecture, what ships in the
# image, the privilege boundary, and the pipeline that reaches users' machines.
#
# !! SETUP REQUIRED !!  The handle below must resolve to a real GitHub user or
# team with write access, otherwise GitHub silently applies NO review
# requirement and this file becomes decorative. After creating the team, verify
# with: gh api 'repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors'   (run inside this repo)
# Branch protection on `main` must also have "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled — CODEOWNERS alone enforces nothing.

# Settled law. Changing an ADR is an owner decision, never an agent's (PRD 0.1).
/docs/adr/                  @ReclaimExperience/owners
/docs/PRD.md                @ReclaimExperience/owners

# What ships in the image. Removals in particular can silently break drivers.
/os/packages.yml            @ReclaimExperience/owners

# The privilege boundary (ADR-015). Three custom polkit actions exist in total.
/os/rootfs/usr/etc/polkit-1/    @ReclaimExperience/owners
/os/rootfs/usr/share/polkit-1/  @ReclaimExperience/owners
/docs/security-notes.md         @ReclaimExperience/owners

# The pipeline that reaches users' machines, and image signing policy (ADR-014).
/ci/                                        @ReclaimExperience/owners
/.github/workflows/                         @ReclaimExperience/owners
/os/rootfs/usr/etc/containers/policy.json   @ReclaimExperience/owners

# The gates themselves. Rule R-E: budgets are laws; you never edit the gate.
/tests/lint/                @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/perf/                @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/privacy/             @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/security/            @ReclaimExperience/owners
